1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,600
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,360
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,920
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED TO DEFAME
OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,960
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

5
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,520
Gun, get in!

6
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,760
Miss Rada, you let him get away.

7
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,720
Find out everything about her.

8
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,840
Starting from the day her parents died.
I want to know how Seehan found her.

9
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,600
<i>Her father was a cop.</i>

10
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:44,000
And he didn't die in an accident.
It was actually murder.

11
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:47,240
<i>I need to talk to you.</i>
<i>I'll send you the location.</i>

12
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,320
<i>He seems to love you so much.</i>

13
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,240
What about you? Do you love him?

14
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,160
You always taught me

15
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,320
never to love the enemy.

16
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:27,520
His life for my new life.

17
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:46,040
I thought you asked me here for revenge.

18
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,400
If I wanted to kill you,

19
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,880
I wouldn't be standing here.

20
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:59,640
Aren't you afraid
I'd bring people to kill you?

21
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,000
If you really wanted me dead,

22
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,960
I wouldn't have survived that day.

23
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,120
Why did you ask me to meet?

24
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:19,160
I investigated your parents.

25
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,440
They didn't die in an accident.

26
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,960
They were murdered.

27
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,280
You have to run, sweetie. Run.

28
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,280
Don't be afraid. Sweetie!

29
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,840
Thun. Thun!

30
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,120
Thun!

31
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,560
Thun!

32
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,520
Dad!

33
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,160
<i>Your father was gathering evidence…</i>

34
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,640
Dad!

35
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,360
-<i>…on border scammers.</i>
-Dad…

36
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,560
And everything…

37
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,640
points to Seehan.

38
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,040
That's not true.

39
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,040
Seehan didn't adopt you

40
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,640
out of love.

41
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:22,320
He just wanted to turn you
into a tool he could use.

42
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:27,080
What are you saying? You're framing him.

43
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,920
He raised you for over 20 years.

44
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,200
I understand if you don't believe me.

45
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:40,480
Here's all the intel I got.

46
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:42,360
It's all in here.

47
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,840
I'm not asking you to believe me.

48
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,440
But I want you to believe the evidence.

49
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,960
I got this from the cop
who's hunting me down.

50
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:06,840
Rada.

51
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,760
I didn't come here to hurt you.

52
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,600
I don't want to see you
used by him anymore.

53
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,320
You once told me

54
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,920
your dream was to live a simple life

55
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,400
with someone by your side.

56
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,040
Is your life right now

57
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,760
really what you want?

58
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,440
I know…

59
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:42,160
the man who gave you
a new life is important.

60
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,320
But if one day you find out he's the one

61
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,200
who destroyed your life
in the first place…

62
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:51,640
would you still choose him?

63
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:59,200
We only die once.

64
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:03,600
That's why I chose this path.

65
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
I never feared death before.

66
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:15,840
But after meeting you…

67
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,200
you changed my heart.

68
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,120
Even though I deceived you,

69
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,960
you still agreed to meet me.

70
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,320
I want you to know.

71
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,520
No matter what happens,

72
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,120
I still love you.

73
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,840
And you.

74
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,480
Did you ever truly love me?

75
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,440
This might be the only thing

76
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,440
I've never lied to you about.

77
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,760
<i>Whenever I was near you,</i>

78
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,160
<i>I felt warm…</i>

79
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,680
<i>and safe.</i>

80
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:44,120
<i>Every moment I spent with you…</i>

81
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,480
<i>I was my truest self.</i>

82
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,280
<i>I can't even remember</i>

83
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,440
<i>how many times…</i>

84
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:00,640
<i>I smiled…</i>

85
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,840
<i>and laughed when I was with you.</i>

86
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,200
Those were…

87
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,360
the happiest days of my life.

88
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,280
I'm glad

89
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,640
I got to be with you.

90
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,600
Do you love me?

91
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:48,760
I…

92
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,440
I love you very much.

93
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,880
I won't let anyone kill you.

94
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,240
<i>I promise you…</i>

95
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,960
<i>I'm willing to give up everything.</i>

96
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,480
<i>But you must kill him.</i>

97
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,200
He's finally dead.

98
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,360
It's finally over, sir.

99
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,880
What about Miss Rada, sir?

100
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,200
She'll be back soon.

101
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,960
Gun.

102
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,240
Gun.

103
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,400
Damn you.

104
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,680
Always find ways to get me in deep shit.

105
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,000
Hey, wait. Gun.

106
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,160
Listen to me.

107
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,320
Rada will never turn against Seehan.

108
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,400
He's raised her since she was a child.

109
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,440
She's completely brainwashed by him.

110
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:07,280
You don't know Rada like I do.

111
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,560
Gun.

112
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:14,640
How many days were you even with her?

113
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,480
With some people,

114
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:20,200
you don't need much time
to know what kind of person they are.

115
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:33,200
I don't know if Rada truly loves you.

116
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:41,000
But Seehan definitely knows that
you love her.

117
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,720
That's why he sent his daughter.

118
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:49,120
You and Rada will never end up together.

119
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:56,080
We'll find another way to kill Seehan.

120
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:06,920
This time, I'll do the shooting for you.

121
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,280
How did you know I was here?

122
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,320
Gun sent me the location.

123
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,120
Gun sent you the location?

124
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,040
He said he was going to turn himself in.

125
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,960
Where is he now?

126
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:54,240
He's dead.

127
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,000
What are you saying?

128
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,880
My friend just died.

129
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,120
You think I'm in the mood for jokes?

130
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,440
Gun wanted Rada to take him
to kill Seehan.

131
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,960
But she chose Seehan.

132
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,400
She's probably

133
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,240
taken his corpse to Seehan by now.

134
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,040
Take him away.

135
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,680
Hey, I'm not going!

136
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,480
Let go! I'm going to avenge Gun!

137
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,720
You have to go.

138
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:30,920
If you want revenge,

139
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:34,080
you have to help me
nail them the right way.

140
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,040
Tell me everything you know.

141
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,800
I'll use the evidence against them.

142
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,880
You still believe?

143
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,600
You still believe in this system?

144
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,000
Do you really think you can catch them?

145
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,080
Yeah!

146
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,080
Aut.

147
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,280
Secure the entire area.
Collect all evidence.

148
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,000
-Yes, sir.
-Let's go.

149
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,600
I'm not going!

150
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,520
Go!

151
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,560
There's nothing wrong with the system.

152
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,720
The problem is the people using it.

153
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:20,480
People like you are the problem.

154
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,280
You're exploiting the law

155
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,920
and using your power
to force good people into evil.

156
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,720
Still running your mouth, huh?

157
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:34,720
Take him with us.

158
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,160
Hey, stop right there.

159
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:37,920
Ma'am.

160
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:43,080
He's in my custody.
Where are you taking him?

161
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:47,840
I worked with Paisan and Decha.

162
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,360
They're now dead.

163
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,640
Someone has to take responsibility.

164
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,000
But this is my job.

165
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,480
I'll prosecute him myself.

166
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,240
I like you.

167
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:03,280
You new-generation guys
are straightforward.

168
00:17:04,119 --> 00:17:07,400
But in the real world, you can't
get ahead on principles alone.

169
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:12,920
Hand him over to me,
and I'll ensure your bright future.

170
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,400
Trust me.

171
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:19,400
In just a few years,

172
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:23,920
your career will take a massive leap,
leaving your peers in the dust.

173
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,200
The future depends on your decision.

174
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:32,000
And if I don't do as you say?

175
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,280
You've served a long time.

176
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:40,080
You know exactly what will happen.

177
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:55,040
You said it yourself.

178
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,240
Police have a duty
to protect what's right.

179
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:04,480
Not serve the people in power like her.

180
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,000
In the end,

181
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,160
you made the same choice.

182
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:22,680
Don't be mad at me, man.

183
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,120
I can't survive on my own
in this corrupt system.

184
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,720
Gun once told me something, too.

185
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,840
In a shady world like this,

186
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,320
you've got to be shady too.

187
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,680
Go.

188
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:57,520
Not only do you know the law inside out,

189
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:00,360
but you also adapt
much faster than I expected.

190
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:05,040
I'm impressed.

191
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,760
After this job, I'll bring you over
to work with me.

192
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,560
Take him.

193
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,080
Where are you going, Boss?

194
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,800
To see Gun's body.

195
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,720
You don't trust Miss Rada, sir?

196
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:48,320
People who trust easily don't live long.

197
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,760
I raised Rada. I know

198
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:56,280
people's feelings can change very quickly.

199
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:03,240
In this world,
I never trust anyone but myself.

200
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,880
I'm handling the body.

201
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,480
Did you really need
to come see it yourself?

202
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:54,840
Well,

203
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:59,480
I wanted to see the face of the guy
who loved causing me so much trouble.

204
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:05,600
What happens inside

205
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:08,600
should stay within the family.

206
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,000
Dad.

207
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:03,440
Do you have any secrets
you want to tell me?

208
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,680
Why would you ask me that?

209
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,440
I kept something from you.

210
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,160
And I feel guilty.

211
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:18,840
I loved Gun.

212
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,680
He was sincere,

213
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,520
straightforward.

214
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,760
I don't fall in love easily.

215
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:35,400
But he made me feel like I mattered.

216
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:36,960
I understand.

217
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:41,600
He was a man of ideals,

218
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:46,800
and more importantly,
he loved his family very much.

219
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:50,120
I don't think it's strange

220
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,440
that you developed feelings for him
after being so close to him.

221
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,480
But one thing surprises me.

222
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,840
You said you loved him so much.

223
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,960
Why did you agree to kill him then?

224
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:13,360
Because you always taught me

225
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:17,320
never to forget who gave me life.

226
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,920
I've told you everything in my heart.

227
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:26,720
Is there anything you want to tell me?

228
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:33,120
Actually, I do have something
I want to tell you too.

229
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:36,760
Rada.

230
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:41,520
Even though you are adopted…

231
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,720
I love you very much.

232
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:51,760
I love you like my own flesh and blood.

233
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,880
When this is over,
come back and live with me.

234
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:05,400
We'll go back to how things were.

235
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:42,320
I gave you an out, but you didn't take it.

236
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:46,280
You chose to be my enemy instead.

237
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:53,800
Don't worry. Your soul won't be lonely.

238
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,440
Your friend will be joining you soon.

239
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:01,360
You should actually thank me

240
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,720
for sending your friend to join you.

241
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:10,160
Dad, what are you doing?

242
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,920
I'll never be able to sleep

243
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:18,000
if I don't kill him with my own hands.

244
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:24,000
I have to kill him myself,
just to be absolutely sure.

245
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:42,960
I won't die until you die first.

246
00:25:44,280 --> 00:25:46,280
Hey!

247
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:55,000
I'll never die

248
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:57,440
as long as you're still breathing.

249
00:25:58,720 --> 00:25:59,680
Shoot me.

250
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,120
I told you to shoot.

251
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:06,280
Are you crazy?

252
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:08,080
Listen to me.

253
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:12,320
Seehan doesn't trust anyone easily.
Especially enemies.

254
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:17,440
You have to trick him
into believing you really killed me.

255
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,320
Why do I have to do that?

256
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:24,080
Because if he thinks I'm dead,

257
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,480
he'll definitely come
to see my body himself.

258
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,800
What if I mess up and kill you?

259
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:33,600
You won't mess up.

260
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:36,080
I trust your skills.

261
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:40,000
What if things go wrong?

262
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:42,240
At least…

263
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:47,000
I'll die at the hands

264
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:50,000
of the woman I love.

265
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:01,800
Rada, give me the gun.
Give it to me, dear. Quickly.

266
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:05,800
Rada…

267
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,720
I don't know what he told you,

268
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:12,440
but he lied to you. Don't believe him!

269
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:13,440
Give me the gun.

270
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:17,800
How did my parents die?

271
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:20,480
It was an accident.

272
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:23,520
Ouch!

273
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:38,640
Don't lie to me again.
I asked how my parents died!

274
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,160
A gun alone won't break down the door.

275
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,480
Go get the gear. Go!

276
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,640
I…

277
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:06,040
I killed them.

278
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:08,480
I killed them myself.

279
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,840
Sweetie! Sweetie!

280
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,160
My girl.

281
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:24,120
It's okay. You have to run, sweetie. Run.

282
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:27,880
Don't be afraid. Sweetie! Sweetie!

283
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:30,760
<i>Back then,</i>

284
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:34,360
<i>they were going to come after me</i>
<i>for buying mule accounts</i>

285
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:37,040
<i>to run cross-border internet lines.</i>

286
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,720
Found them, Boss.

287
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:40,960
<i>They were going to come after me.</i>

288
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:46,640
Rada.

289
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,720
I had no choice.

290
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:52,120
Forgive me.

291
00:28:53,280 --> 00:28:54,600
Please forgive me, dear.

292
00:28:57,600 --> 00:28:59,280
If I hadn't regretted it,

293
00:29:00,080 --> 00:29:01,920
I wouldn't have adopted you.

294
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:09,400
Forgive me. Forgive your dad.

295
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:15,760
Dad? A real father

296
00:29:15,840 --> 00:29:17,680
would never force his child
to do the evil,

297
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:19,760
dirty things you do!

298
00:29:21,320 --> 00:29:23,440
You didn't raise me

299
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,240
because you loved me.

300
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:30,080
You raised me to do your dirty work!

301
00:29:32,720 --> 00:29:35,560
Every time I called you Dad,

302
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:38,800
I felt so pathetic!

303
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:42,520
<i>I don't think Miss Rada is the same</i>
<i>this time around.</i>

304
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:45,320
In her previous assignments,

305
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:49,640
Rada used her feminine charms
to close every deal.

306
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:52,680
She's smart,

307
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:56,240
capable, quick-witted,

308
00:29:57,280 --> 00:29:58,720
and a survivor.

309
00:29:59,240 --> 00:30:01,600
She has all the qualities

310
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:03,480
that are incredibly useful to me.

311
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:06,200
Just like you said,

312
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:10,840
Rada came back different

313
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:13,400
this time.

314
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,800
<i>I've raised her since she was little.</i>

315
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,320
<i>I can tell.</i>

316
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:20,840
My dear child.

317
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:33,200
Please talk some sense into her, sir.

318
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:36,160
She's too grown to listen to me now.

319
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:40,600
For someone who knows this much,
there are only two options.

320
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:46,760
The first is to keep using her
to advance our work.

321
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:48,880
And the second?

322
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:50,200
Get rid of her.

323
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:53,000
She knows too much.

324
00:31:03,520 --> 00:31:07,120
You've never loved anyone but yourself!

325
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:10,400
Don't, dear. Don't. Don't do it.

326
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:14,240
Wait, wait! Stop!

327
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:19,720
What do you want? Tell me what you want!

328
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:21,800
Money?

329
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:25,200
Power? You want it?

330
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:28,280
I can give you everything! Let me go. Now!

331
00:31:28,360 --> 00:31:30,240
Your money and your power

332
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:33,320
are worthless to me.

333
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:39,080
The only thing of value is your life.

334
00:31:55,600 --> 00:31:56,560
Rada.

335
00:31:58,080 --> 00:31:59,080
No, dear.

336
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:00,720
Rada.

337
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:05,640
Don't. Don't, dear.

338
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:08,720
Rada. No.

339
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:19,360
-Boss! Go!
-Let's go.

340
00:32:20,120 --> 00:32:21,080
Come on!

341
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:39,760
That's enough.

342
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:20,679
‎Move!

343
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:27,639
Go.

344
00:34:40,239 --> 00:34:41,560
What are you going to do with me?

345
00:34:43,199 --> 00:34:46,520
Going to court is a waste of time.
I'll pass judgment myself.

346
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:30,560
You've got a big mouth, huh?
Still love running your mouth?

347
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:31,720
Ouch…

348
00:37:28,920 --> 00:37:31,600
<i>If he wants to run,</i>
<i>he'll need to retrieve his hidden cash</i>

349
00:37:31,680 --> 00:37:33,080
<i>to set up a new base abroad.</i>

350
00:37:33,160 --> 00:37:34,760
I won't let this chance slip away.

351
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:41,920
You're really digging your own graves.

352
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,680
<i>Go deal with them right now.</i>

353
00:37:50,160 --> 00:37:51,080
Hey!

354
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:56,800
You're going to get
the one you love killed.

355
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:57,800
-Take this!
-Ouch!

356
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:58,840
Rada!

357
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:01,080
Hit him, then wait for him to get back up.

358
00:38:01,160 --> 00:38:03,320
-Okay?
-Like this?

359
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:04,360
Boom!

360
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,440
Bam!

361
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:06,880
Bam!

362
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:11,120
-Attack.
-I kick. Bam!

363
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:13,400
-Hit him.
-Bam!

364
00:38:13,480 --> 00:38:15,800
Kick me. No need
to wait for me to hit you.

365
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:19,800
-No need to wait. Just kick me back.
-Bam!

366
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:21,360
-Set. Set.
-Ready.

367
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:23,320
And action!

368
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:24,360
Ugh.

369
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:29,360
Cue! Cue!

370
00:38:34,240 --> 00:38:35,520
Cut. Okay.

371
00:38:35,600 --> 00:38:37,000
Esther, are you safe?

372
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:38,240
-No?
-No.

373
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:40,200
-She's not safe.
-Because you…

374
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:42,120
Esther, cover up.

375
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:43,480
Cover your face.

376
00:38:43,560 --> 00:38:45,120
Whoa. What?

377
00:38:45,200 --> 00:38:46,040
Debris?

378
00:38:46,120 --> 00:38:48,440
-You okay?
-Am I?

379
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:49,360
Bring the loaded gun.

380
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:50,360
Where? Your hair?

381
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:52,200
Just some light debris,

382
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:53,680
and only a little.

383
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:54,960
Don't pull it out.

384
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:59,040
-As soon as you turn around…
-Before you do anything…

385
00:38:59,120 --> 00:38:59,960
Four.

386
00:39:03,600 --> 00:39:05,320
<i>-Stay focused. Setting up.</i>
-Set.

387
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:07,360
<i>Make it count.</i>

388
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:08,800
<i>Action!</i>

389
00:39:20,480 --> 00:39:22,000
-That was exhausting.
-Cut!

390
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:23,200
Great job.

391
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:26,440
-Great job.
-What did we even get?

392
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:27,760
-Well done.
-You okay?

393
00:39:27,840 --> 00:39:29,480
-Alright.
-We're done here.

394
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:31,640
-Okay, okay.
-Let's see it.

395
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:33,440
Let's go see it.

396
00:39:35,880 --> 00:39:37,720
You already know how it is.
What do you want?

397
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:41,640
See the guy with a topknot?

398
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:44,840
-Just like Rain in Bloodhounds.
-Wow. Rain?

399
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,480
You tucked your hands.

400
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:22,960
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
